# Codex Prompt: Milestone 2 — Execute AI-Generated Test Cases Using Playwright

Act as a senior Python automation engineer and AI testing architect. Extend the existing AI-powered autonomous testing agent by implementing Milestone 2.

## 1. Objective

Milestone 1 already accepts business requirements and uses an AI model to generate structured JSON test cases.

Now implement a Playwright-based test execution engine that consumes those test cases and executes them against a user-provided web application.

The workflow must be:

Business Requirement
        ↓
Existing Test Case Generator
        ↓
Structured JSON Test Cases
        ↓
Playwright Execution Engine
        ↓
Real Browser Interaction
        ↓
Assertions and Verification
        ↓
Execution Results and Evidence

The application must execute actual browser actions, not merely print the generated test cases.

IMPORTANT: Inspect the current repository and preserve the working Milestone 1 implementation. Reuse existing models, routes, configuration, and services wherever appropriate. Do not rewrite the project from scratch.

## 2. Technology

Use:
- Python
- Existing FastAPI backend, if already implemented
- Playwright for Python
- Pydantic for request and response validation
- pytest for automated testing

Install and configure the required dependencies if they are missing.

Use Chromium as the initial browser.

Keep the implementation modular so Firefox, WebKit, and additional execution capabilities can be added later.

