## 13. Definition of done

Milestone 2 is complete when:

1. I can supply a web application URL and valid test cases.
2. Playwright opens the actual application.
3. The executor performs supported browser actions.
4. Assertions are checked against real browser state.
5. Each test receives an accurate execution status.
6. Failures include useful diagnostic evidence.
7. Unsupported actions never produce false PASS results.
8. Execution timeouts and resource cleanup work correctly.
9. The combined workflow works if implemented.
10. Milestone 1 remains functional.
11. Automated tests pass.
12. Documentation explains how to run the complete workflow.

Start by inspecting the existing codebase and identifying the actual Milestone 1 schema. Implement the executor incrementally, run the tests, fix failures, and summarize the completed work. Do not stop after proposing an architecture.

IMPORTANT: The model generates test plans; Playwright executes them; deterministic assertions determine the actual test outcomes. Never ask the LLM to fabricate execution results.
